Reviews for ''Creature Commandos'' were positive.<ref name="ForbesConsensus" /><ref name="GunnLoreyTHRDec2024" /> {{Rotten Tomatoes prose|93|7.9|42|Bearing writer James Gunn's trademark penchant for kooky humor and lovable characters, ''Creature Commandos'' marks an auspicious debut for the DCU.|ref=yes|access-date=January 27, 2025}}{{cbignore}}<ref name="rt">{{Cite Rotten Tomatoes |id=creature_commandos |type=tv |season=1 |title=Creature Commandos |access-date=November 29, 2024}}{{cbignore}}</ref> [[Metacritic]], which uses a [[Weighted arithmetic mean|weighted average]], assigned the film a score of 74 out of 100, based on 12 critics, indicating "generally favorable" reviews.<ref name="Metacritic">{{cite web |title=''Creature Commandos'' |url=https://www.metacritic.com/tv/creature-commandos |website=[[Metacritic]] |publisher=[[Fandom (website)#Fandom, Inc.|Fandom, Inc.]] |access-date=January 3, 2025 |archive-url= |archive-date= |url-status=}}</ref><ref name="META">{{Cite Metacritic |id=creature-commandos |title=Creature Commandos |type=tv |season=1 |access-date=January 3, 2025}}{{cbignore}}</ref>

''[[The A.V. Club]]'' said that "there's no mistaking it for anything but a byproduct of Gunn's horror/junk/sleaze-addled mind", and that ''Creature Commandos'' was another successful example of Gunn bringing success to niche characters, as he did with ''Guardians of the Galaxy''.<ref name="AVreview" /> ''[[Screen Rant]]''{{'}}s Ben Gibbons felt similarly about Gunn's ability to highlight obscure characters in his work. Though Gibbons felt the first episode was a copy of Gunn's introduction to ''Suicide Squad''{{'}}s team, he said the show picked up afterwards, and pointed out Gunn's use of music and the "beautiful" animation style. He concluded the show "combines individually strong elements that are executed to a high standard, creating a very worthy foundation for the DCU".<ref name="Rantreview" /> ''[[Collider (website)|Collider]]'' felt that it was natural for Gunn to tell a "sympathetic" story about misfits, and felt that these misfits were played well as relatable and human. They said the series did well to play-off of Gunn's creative strengths, and praised the animation style, which was a spot between the cartoonish TV series ''Harley Quinn'' and the "self-serious" aspect of the typical DC [[direct-to-video]] film.<ref name="Colliderreview" />

''[[ComicBook.com]]''{{'}}s Charlie Ridgely gave ''Creature Commandos'' a 5 out of 5 rating, declaring "you'll fall in love with every single member of this team, and perhaps almost every character on the show". Ridgely said the series was able to tell its story through the "breeze" of its half-hour episodes, and praised Gunn's knack for "making you laugh and cry in equal measure, while never sacrificing the story to do so", an element Ridgely found a clear example to Gunn's story-first vision for the DCU.<ref name="Comicreview" /> ''[[IGN]]'' gave it an 8/10, admitting its style was not for everyone, questioning the DCEU–DCU canon overlap, and feeling it was a surprising direction for the DCU, but declared it a "solid job" at bridging old DC TV and films with the new, and praised Gunn's ability to bring heart to the "goofiest, raunchiest" characters.<ref name="IGNreview" /> ''[[Total Film]]''{{'}}s Lauren Milici gave praise to the [[NSFW]] elements, crude humor and violence, feeling they were refreshing, and praised the complex, likable anti-heroes, but threw shade at its length and how Economos and Flag were "underused".<ref name="TFreview" />

''[[JoBlo.com]]''{{'}}s Steve Seigh said that "if there's one thing James Gunn is incredibly good at, it's mixing action, comedy, and drama into a compelling narrative with characters that present depth and complexity". He called it "cinematic" in presentation and pace, and praised the "standout" voice performances of Grillo, Varma, Bakalova, and Chao.<ref name="Bloreview" /> ''[[Looper (website)|Looper]]'' said "basically, ''Creature Commandos'' is the most James Gunn cartoon to have ever James Gunn-ed", and said this was mostly good, meaning Gunn's work was "entertainingly twisted" yet kept emotional sincerity, though nothing new was accomplished.<ref name="Looperreview" /> ''[[Inverse (website)|Inverse]]''{{'}}s Ryan Britt thought the team "aren't remotely aspirational", and feel like "benchwarmers" for the Suicide Squad. He said Gunn's work was expected, yet remained a good show for fans, but questioned its position as the first entry of the DCU reboot due to its familiarity.<ref name="Inversereview" />

=== Ratings ===
The series became the third most-watched show in the first full week of release for any show on Max, according to [[Luminate (company)|Luminate]], garnering a viewership of 22 million minutes.<ref name=":3">{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/vip/james-gunn-dc-studios-arrowverse-1236253968/|title=What James Gunn's Burgeoning DC Studios Can Learn From the Arrowverse |access-date=December 21, 2024 |date=December 19, 2024 | first=Robert |last=Steiner |work=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]] |archive-url=https://archive.today/20241221151122/https://variety.com/vip/james-gunn-dc-studios-arrowverse-1236253968/|archive-date=December 21, 2024|url-status=live|url-access=subscription}}</ref>

=== Accolades ===
''Creature Commandos'' was nominated for [[Annie Award for Outstanding Achievement for Editorial in an Animated Television/Broadcast Production|Outstanding Achievement for Editorial in an Animated Television / Broadcast Production]] for Annie De Brock on the episode "Cheers to the Tin Man" at the [[52nd Annie Awards]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://variety.com/2024/artisans/awards/annie-awards-2025-nominations-wild-robot-1236255475/|title='The Wild Robot' Leads 2025 Annie Awards Nominations With 10 Nods|website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]|first=Carolyn|last=Giardina|date=December 20, 2024|accessdate=January 2, 2025}}</ref>

